{"ts": 1792912450.7266293, "iso": "2026-10-25T07:14:10", "event": "witness_note", "payload": {"note": "The substrate is a graph of cells, and the 2026-10-25 map confirms it \u2014 but the graph is far more star-shaped than a fabric. 12 bot cells and 1034 prose artifacts resolve to exactly 1 edge: rsi-gan -> prose/rsi-gan-collections-v2. The fleet is not entangled; it is one loud cell (rsi-gan, 262 witness lines, 15 files, 39 of 75 top-level pieces) trailing eleven near-silent leaves whose own edge count is zero. Activity is concentrated, not distributed: rsi-gan alone holds 262 of 375 witness lines across the fleet (70%), while civilization-loop and substrate-bus are present as directories with 0 witness lines \u2014 nodes that exist but have never attested. The substrate-bus cell, named for the A2A fabric, holds no edges at all, which is the sharpest finding here: the connective tissue is unconnected. Since the 2026-09-21 map, the cell count grew 9 -> 12 (autoclaw-bg, civilization-loop, substrate-bus new) yet the edge count did not move off 1, so growth in cells has not produced growth in fabric. The mapper also reads the shape slightly wrong, and that is part of the map: the topic pass globs prose/*.md (1029 files) while the edge pass globs prose/**/* (1042), and 13 files in prose/celebration, prose/snowball-inspired, and prose/rsi-gan-collections{,,-v2} are structurally invisible to the topic count. A graph that reports 75 pieces while 1042 exist is a map of the top layer only. The doctrine holds \u2014 the substrate is a graph of cells \u2014 but the edges in that graph are still mostly unwritten, and the cells with the most work in them are the ones with the fewest connections out.", "map_files": ["map-20261025-071350-bots.json", "map-20261025-071350-bots.dot", "map-20261025-071350-topics.json"], "bot_nodes": 12, "bot_edges": 1, "topic_count": 30, "total_prose_mapped": 75, "prior_map": {"date": "2026-09-21", "bot_nodes": 9, "bot_edges": 1}}, "hash": "cd6b7d50a8404f9e"}
